\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces  Summary of different SM signal models. The MC samples are from full Run 2 yearly productions (2016, 2017 and 2018) assuming $m_{\rm  H} = 125.0\GeV $. Luminosity averaged fiducial acceptance ($\mathcal  {A}_{\rm  fid}$) defined the fraction of events passing fiducial phase space selections, reconstruction efficiency ($\epsilon $) represented by the ratio of reconstructed to accepted events. Also, $f_{\rm  nonfid}$ which are reconstructed events but does not pass fiducial phase space definition at generator level. Values are obtained using 13\hspace  {0.25em plus 0.125em minus 0.08em}\ignorespaces TeV signal models and the uncertainties shown are only statistical uncertainties.  \relax }}{13}{table.caption.34}}
\newlabel{tab:summarySMfullRun2}{{1.2}{13}{Summary of different SM signal models. The MC samples are from full Run 2 yearly productions (2016, 2017 and 2018) assuming $m_{\rm H} = 125.0\GeV $. Luminosity averaged fiducial acceptance ($\mathcal {A}_{\rm fid}$) defined the fraction of events passing fiducial phase space selections, reconstruction efficiency ($\epsilon $) represented by the ratio of reconstructed to accepted events. Also, $f_{\rm nonfid}$ which are reconstructed events but does not pass fiducial phase space definition at generator level. Values are obtained using 13~TeV signal models and the uncertainties shown are only statistical uncertainties.  \relax }{table.caption.34}{}}
